<template>
    <heading>Startup code</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>startup</li>
        <li>module</li>
        <li>command</li>
        <li>dialog</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>This module script runs after the browser has parsed the document, so the dialog templates are available. The earlier classic script has already constructed the <code>window.LP5</code> units.</p>
        <p>After installing error handlers, startup enumerates <code>Object.values(window.LP5)</code> in property order and synchronously invokes each object's <code>startup()</code> function when present. Hooks run as methods of their unit. A thrown exception stops enumeration and prevents the initial command; async hooks are not awaited by this simple lifecycle. Operations uses its hook to compile and install the machine, so compilation errors occur after reporting is ready.</p>
        <p>Startup dispatches a <code>ModalDialog</code> command with the logical operation key <code>SelectCreateProject</code>. The base handler uses that key to call the dialog-specific operation. The dialog template's DOM id is also <code>SelectCreateProject</code>.</p>
        <p>Before dispatching startup, install handlers for uncaught errors and unhandled Promise rejections. The first failure displays its message as plain text in a permanent modal; later failures leave that first report intact. Escape cannot dismiss it, and there are no application controls for recovery. The user must reload the entire page through the browser. Console reports remain enabled. This first cut blocks ordinary UI interaction but does not cancel queued commands or ongoing async work, and cannot catch failures before this module installs the handlers.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>Startup code</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
<script type="module">
    let errorDialog;

    function showMessage(message) {
        if (errorDialog) return;
        errorDialog = document.createElement("dialog");
        errorDialog.setAttribute("role", "alertdialog");
        errorDialog.setAttribute("aria-labelledby", "LP5-FatalError-title");
        errorDialog.style.cssText = "max-width: 32rem; padding: 1.25rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere";

        const title = document.createElement("h2");
        title.id = "LP5-FatalError-title";
        title.textContent = "Execution failed";
        const detail = document.createElement("p");
        detail.textContent = message;
        detail.style.whiteSpace = "pre-wrap";
        const instruction = document.createElement("p");
        instruction.textContent = "Reload the entire page using your browser before continuing.";
        errorDialog.append(title, detail, instruction);
        errorDialog.addEventListener("cancel", event => event.preventDefault());
        document.body.append(errorDialog);
        errorDialog.showModal();
    }

    window.addEventListener("error", event => {
        showMessage(event.error?.message ?? event.message);
    });
    window.addEventListener("unhandledrejection", event => {
        showMessage(event.reason?.message ?? String(event.reason));
    });

    for (const unit of Object.values(window.LP5)) {
        if (unit && typeof unit === "object" && typeof unit.startup === "function")
            unit.startup();
    }

    window.LP5.controller.dispatch({
        name: "ModalDialog",
        dialogName: "SelectCreateProject"
    });
</script>
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
